<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">A Theology of Liberation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1971">1971</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Teología de la liberación</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A Theology of Liberation is a book by the Peruvian priest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavo-gutierrez">Gustavo Gutiérrez</a>, published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in 1971 as Teología de la liberación and in English in 1973. It interpreted Christian faith from the standpoint of the poor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-america">Latin America</a> and called on the church to commit itself to their liberation from poverty and oppression. The founding text of liberation theology, it influenced Catholic thinking far beyond the continent and drew criticism from the Vatican in the 1980s.</p></div>
